That's fine for the early game, but no more unnecessary risks.  The
game you have now is an ascension waiting to happen as long as you
don't get careless.

And like David said, that means worrying about *immediate* survival,
not survival in Gehennom.  If you can get to Gehennom, you can beat
Gehennom; it's all mazes so monsters can't really surround you.
Just have a plan for dealing with Demogorgon.  He can be summoned
by Yeenoghu and Orcus, so don't hang around them if you can't kill
them quick.  Stop worrying about what artifacts you'll get.  You've
got a silver saber.  If you don't have Mojo yet, sacrifice for Mojo.
Then get the Orb of Fate.  Until you get an AoLS, dual-wield Mojo
and the silver saber and wear the amulet of reflection.  When you
get an AoLS, put it on and wield the shield of reflection and
Mojo if you're fighting something that isn't a demon and the silver
saber if you're fighting something that is a demon.

And then *stop worrying about artifacts.*  If you find a nice one,
great.  If you have some spare wishes and want to try for one, go
for it.  But first get a source of MR and some good armor.  If you
have wishes to spare but don't think you'll get an artifact from them,
that just means you can wish for SDSM and a cloak of MR so you don't
have to choose between an AoLS and twoweaponing.  Artifacts are not
as important as you think they are.

If you don't aren't high enough level to enter the quest, dance
with foocubi until you are.  Find a sink, clear the level, then
kick it until one shows up.  Have telepathy and a blindfold/towel
so you can see where the foocubus teleports to and if anything
else shows up on the level.  Do this on as high a dlvl as possible
so the monsters will be easier.

Always, *always* have an escape item.  You've got teleport control,
and the Orb of Fate does levelport when invoked.  You can go straight
to your stash (or the level right below it if the stash is in
Sokoban.)  Just make sure you wait 150 turns or so after invoking it
so it'll stand a good chance of being recharged the next time you need
it.  Honestly, with teleport control, the Orb is as good as the Eye of
A. for escaping.  And the Orb is *guaranteed* for the Valkyrie as long
as you're willing to go for it.  Cursed scrolls of teleport will also
work as levelport, so always have one of them just in case the Orb
isn't recharged when you need it.

Read up on drawbridges before you do the quest.  They're safe as long
as you know how to deal with them.  So know how to deal with them.


